plugin-db (0.4.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * release: plugin-db 0.4.7, the spec changelog names the floors that moved
  * release: plugin-db 0.4.7 (0.4.6 to 0.4.7), a patch, re-cut on current main
  * formats_test: state the unloaded arm's one assumption
  * An unreadable domain is PDB_ERR_FORMATS, never "no address", and the fill
    is once
  * Red: an unreadable domain is its own result, not "no address"
  * Separate the protocol's headers from the codes header, one translation
    unit each
  * Red: no translation unit sees both the protocol's vocabulary and the
    codes header
  * PLUGIN_DB_ADDRESS_FORMATS moves to the plugin-db domain, read through the
    loader
  * Red: PLUGIN_DB_ADDRESS_FORMATS lives only in the plugin-db domain
  * Document make render-domain as a release step
  * The formats domain takes its version from VERSION and keeps its codes
    stable
  * Red: the formats domain's version and codes are stable
  * CI: the words job installs the loader's command for make test-domain
  * Publish the address formats as the plugin-db domain, rendered from
    data/db.json
  * Red: plugin-db's address formats as a domain item the loader opens
  * schema addresses: the store schema takes
    https://openmixer.org/schema/plugin-db/store.schema.json as its $id, not
    a code-hosting address

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:00:42 +0000
